# What a verification run leaves behind.
#
# scripts/verify-photoroom.ts writes the pictures it got back so they can be
# looked at — that is the whole point of it, since a mode can return HTTP 200
# and still have ignored what it was asked. They are evidence for one
# afternoon, not source: sandbox output with another company's watermark
# across it, megabytes of it, regenerated whenever anyone re-runs the check.
#
# The script drops a .gitignore into whatever --out folder it is given, so
# any future run ignores itself whatever it is called. These are the ones
# that already existed before it learned to.
apps/api/photoroom-check/
apps/api/angles/
apps/api/check2/
apps/api/check4/
